{"doc":"Offline oracle: real qiskit-gym 0.4.1 envs (train.make_env: from_coupling_map, QUMO basis, add_inverts/add_perms default True) and the real twisterl 0.5.1 collector / evaluate on FIXED explicit f32 weights (torch layout, flat row-major, as in policy_forward.json; BasicPolicy E=12, common [8], torch default init x3). Collector: gamma = lambda = 0.995, 5000 single-episode collect() calls per (config, difficulty); a collected row is one visited state (the terminal state is recorded, its mask is all -1e10 iff solved). Variables per row: rets, advs (twisterl GAE), values, rewards (env.reward() of the state), old_lp = l_a - logsumexp(l) of the recorded MASKED logits in f32 (0.0 on an all-masked row), all_masked (1 on a row whose logits are all -1e10). 'stats' gives for each variable the pooled row mean and a cluster-robust standard error: with per-episode sum S_e and row count L_e, mean = sum S / sum L and se = sqrt(sum (S_e - mean*L_e)^2) / sum L. 'std_rows' is the plain row standard deviation. len_hist maps episode length (rows) to the number of episodes; solved_episode_fraction is the fraction of episodes whose terminal row is all-masked (se binomial, floor 0.25/N). Test: two-sample z = (m_mojo - m_ref) / sqrt(se_ref^2 + se_mojo^2) with se_mojo from the same estimator, |z| <= 4. Evaluate: 20 blocks of 1000 episodes (pauli_network line:3 difficulty 16: 200 blocks deterministic and 1000 blocks sampled, regenerated with the same weights and protocol because the 20-block sampled run had drawn 2 successes against an expected 11; 'successes' is the integer count), evaluate(deterministic=True, num_searches=1) and evaluate(deterministic=False, num_searches=10); 'success' = mean success rate, 'reward' = mean summed env.reward() of every visited state including the initial and the final one; se_blocks = std of block means / sqrt(blocks); se_binomial = sqrt(max(p(1-p), 0.25/N) / N). Use max(se_blocks, se_binomial) for success. twist_counts (in 'collector') are the recorde